<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inanna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inanna was the Sumerian goddess of love, war and fertility, identified with the Akkadian Ishtar. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enheduanna">Enheduanna</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a> and high priestess at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, composed hymns to her and is regarded as the first named author in history. Her cult forms part of the religious background of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>.</p></div>
